  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=-5\\sqrt[8]{4x+9}+5.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To find the roots of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-5\\sqrt[8]{4x+9}+5=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[8]{4x+9}+5 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[8]{4x+9} & =-5 \\\\ \\sqrt[8]{4x+9} & =1 \\\\ {(\\sqrt[8]{4x+9})}^{8} & ={1}^{8} \\\\ 4x+9 & =1 \\\\ 4x & =-8 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[8]{4\\cdot (-2)+9}+5 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[8]{1}+5 & =0 \\\\ -5\\cdot 1+5 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-2.$",
